able form.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"GOLDEN_THREAD_INFORMATION_CONTROLS","direct_score_input":false},{"row":91,"status":"PASS_BSR_RESIDENT_COMPLAINT_ROUTE","source":"BSR resident complaint guidance","url":"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/complain-about-a-building-safety-risk-in-a-high-rise-building","verified":"Residents should first raise building-safety concerns with the accountable person or principal accountable person and can refer unresolved matters to BSR.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"RESIDENT_COMPLAINT_ESCALATION","direct_score_input":false},{"row":92,"status":"PASS_BSR_COMPLAINT_EVIDENCE","source":"BSR resident complaint guidance","url":"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/complain-about-a-building-safety-risk-in-a-high-rise-building","verified":"Helpful evidence includes final responses, photographs, video, emails, letters and records of planned or completed actions.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"COMPLAINT_EVIDENCE_SCHEMA","direct_score_input":false},{"row":93,"status":"PASS_BSR_COMPLAINT_TRIAGE","source":"BSR resident complaint guidance","url":"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/complain-about-a-building-safety-risk-in-a-high-rise-building","verified":"BSR decides whether a referred complaint is relevant and may advise, investigate or redirect it to another regulator.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"COMPLAINT_TRIAGE_METHOD","direct_score_input":false},{"row":94,"status":"PASS_RIDDOR_WORK_RELATED_AND_REPORTABLE","source":"HSE RIDDOR incident types","url":"https://www.hse.gov.uk/riddor/types-of-reportable-incidents.htm","verified":"A RIDDOR report is required only when an accident is work-related and causes a reportable injury.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"RIDDOR_DUAL_CONDITION","direct_score_input":false},{"row":95,"status":"PASS_RIDDOR_DEATH_SCOPE","source":"HSE RIDDOR incident types","url":"https://www.hse.gov.uk/riddor/types-of-reportable-incidents.htm","verified":"A death caused by a work-related accident is reportable, except suicide.","quality_score"